TIP:  The whole song follows a nifty little chord sequence that takes a little concentration but is pretty easy to play.  So start with (Em).  From there spread your fingers open, top finger moves up one string, bottom finger moves down one string.  That’s (D6/9).  From there you keep the bottom finger where it is but move the top finger back to where it was on the 5th string.  That’s (Esus). 
    

